y for a higher degree.\nPostgraduate\nJoin us on our journey as we explore new discoveries and formulate ground breaking research.\nResearch & Enterprise\nOur highly-ranked school generates world-class research and welcomes new collaborations.\nFacilities\nOur cutting edge facilities allow us to reach out to the scientific community and provide education excellence with impact.\nSchool Intranet\nInformation for Staff Students Affiliates & Visitors\nOur People\nMeet our academics and researchers\nStudent Initiatives & Societies\nMonash Chemical Society, CHAMPS and Society of Chemistry Students\nExchange programs\nLearn about our collaborations with overseas universities and laboratories\nQuick links\nAbout Us\nSchool Committees\nPhD Scholarship Opportunities\nAlumni\nNews & Events\nEquity, Diversity and Inclusion\nFollow us\nLinkedIn\nTwitter\nGeneral enquiries\nEmail: chem-enquiries@monash.edu\nTelephone: +61 3 9905 4548\nLatest news from Chemistry\nMonash chemist recognised with 2026 RACI Welcome Award\nMonash Science chemist Dr Felipe Garc\u00eda has been named the recipient of the 2026 Royal Australian Chemical Institute (RACI) Welcome Award, recognising his contributions to Australian chemistry since joining Monash in 2024.\nCHEMISTRY\nNew electrode design breaks key barrier to greener ammonia production\nA new approach to producing ammonia using renewable electricity has overcome a fundamental energy limitation of the technology, opening new possibilities for cleaner and potentially more cost-effective production of one of the world\u2019s most\nCHEMISTRY\nFive Monash Science researchers awarded $5.7 million in ARC Future Fellowships\nThe ARC Future Fellowships will support researchers to advance research spanning climate resilience, renewable energy, plant productivity, fluid dynamics and stellar astrophysics.\nRESEARCH\nGlobal recognition for Monash chemists driving innovations in clean energy storage\nCongratulations to the Thermal Energy Storage Group from the Monash University School of Chemistry on being awarded a 2026 Royal Society of Chemistry Horizon Prize.\nCHEMISTRY\nMonash Master of Food Science and Agribusiness trains students to think like industry, using real-time consumer insight\nIn most food science courses, students develop a product first and only later test whether consumers actually want it. But at Monash University, that sequence is being flipped.\nCHEMISTRY\nView more articles\nWe acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians\nCOMMUNITY\nFaculties\nLocations\nDiversity and inclusion\nSafety and security\nSustainability\nRESOURCES\nImportant dates\nHow to apply\nA-Z index\nPolicy Bank\nFAQs\nCONTACT\nContact us\nCampus maps\nJobs at Monash\nRecruit a student\nPay online\nNEWS\nLatest news\nMonash Lens\nPodcasts\nA Different Lens\nMonash Life\nON OUR SITE\nCurrent students\nStaff intranet\nSite map\nREGISTERED AUSTRALIAN UNIVERSITY\nABN: 12 377 614 012\nTEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140\nCRICOS PROVIDER NUMBER\nMonash University: 00008C\nMonash College: 01857J\nAUTHORISED BY\nExecutive Director, Marketing\nWebsite feedback\nLast updated: Feb 2026\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer & copyright\nTerms & conditions\nData privacy & cyber security\nData Consent Settings\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Monash University\nWe use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions\nAccept all\nCookie settings", "links": [["Home", "https://www.monash.edu/science"], ["Courses", "https://www.monash.edu/study/courses"], ["Monash Online", "https://online.monash.edu/"], ["Library", "https://www.monash.edu/library"], ["Donate", "https://www.monash.edu/giving"], ["Science", "https://www.monash.edu/science"], ["About us", "https://www.monash.edu/science/about"], ["About us", "https://www.monash.edu/science/about"], ["Sc